10. Conclusion

We have advanced a rigorous, falsifiable mathematical theory in which coupled human–AI systems function as constrained dynamical systems with attractor landscapes. Local convergence is guaranteed when delays are small and objectives are locally convex; beyond a computable threshold, oscillation and collapse become inevitable. The theory’s predictions are already manifest in recent, independent research from institutions including MIT, CMU, and the Chinese Academy of Sciences, confirming its descriptive and predictive power. We offer the framework as a foundation for the principled design of safe, stable, and self-correcting human–AI collaborations in an increasingly algorithmic world.


